83
00:08:51.720 --> 00:08:59.320
By the end of the summer, I danced myself right down to skin and bones, and I had to stop and go to work before the loafing killed me, Casey recalled.

84
00:08:59.320 --> 00:09:02.520
It may have been the last easy summer of his life.

85
00:09:02.520 --> 00:09:10.680
While Casey had been away, two unlikely forces had begun to undermine Bucktoush's economy a caterpillar and a catalog.

86
00:09:10.680 --> 00:09:13.320
The caterpillar was the spruce budworm.

87
00:09:13.320 --> 00:09:17.960
A single budworm was insignificant, barely longer than a fingernail.

88
00:09:17.960 --> 00:09:20.360
An outbreak of them, however, was not.

89
00:09:20.360 --> 00:09:25.080
They came in the billions, stripping the trees that the sawmills depended on.

90
00:09:25.080 --> 00:09:28.120
Across the county, mills had begun to shut down.

91
00:09:28.120 --> 00:09:30.440
JD's was on borrowed time.

92
00:09:30.440 --> 00:09:34.360
As usable timber dwindled, workers lost hours and wages.

93
00:09:34.360 --> 00:09:40.200
A town that had lived by cutting trees had no easy answer when the forest could no longer feed its mills.

94
00:09:40.200 --> 00:09:42.760
That wasn't the only threat he faced.

95
00:09:42.760 --> 00:09:45.160
The other one came through the mail.

96
00:09:45.160 --> 00:09:56.040
The Eton's catalog offered rural Canadians hundreds of pages of clothing, furniture, tools, equipment, and household goods at prices a village merchant struggled with.

97
00:09:56.040 --> 00:09:58.360
You can think of it like the Sears Catalog.

98
00:09:58.360 --> 00:10:03.000
Eatons didn't need to construct a store or employ people in every small community.

99
00:10:03.000 --> 00:10:08.280
The catalogue turned the post office and railway into its own distribution network.

100
00:10:08.280 --> 00:10:11.960
